    offer_curve_by_group: { cell: "R", ev: "SPP PRICE-FAMILY (2026-09-07) — R: REJECTED as a UNIFORM per-band quadruple, killed by the pre-registered rule-29 STRUCTURAL screen on 2025 even though it IMPROVED both target criteria (C3a +7.2% -> -2.5%, C3b 0.1894 -> 0.1708). Arm = the rules-1/13 AUTHORIZED price-tuning channel, declared ex ante in PRECOMMIT-spp-price-family-2026-09-07.md §4.1: committed 0.845 / econ_low 0.794 / econ_high 1.018 / peak 1.118, ONE config all years, derived load-weighted from SPP's OWN hourly RT LMP and KS/OK delivered gas on the <=$200 surface, applied to the 10 registered classes SPP dispatches; no phys_*, no econ_low_share, no pct_peaking, *_INTERMEDIATE untouched (all three splits False). GATE: G-1 level PASS (LW mean 29.971 -> 27.258, -9.05% vs -10.08% predicted, window [25.47,28.47]); G-3 footprint PASS (non-thermal 0.000%, unserved 90.6 MWh); **G-2 STOP** — the steepening ratio MHR(>95pct)/MHR(25-75pct) moved 1.6214 -> 1.6298, +0.5%, against the required >=1.783 (measured SPP 2.1088). WHY: the arm/control price ratio is 0.9070-0.9151 across the WHOLE load range (0.81 pp spread) — a uniform quadruple applied to every class preserves the between-class merit order, so it is a LEVEL lever, not a SHAPE lever; the surface moved down, it did not rotate. Promoting on the improved residual is the fitted-mechanism selection rule 1 [R-STRUCT] forbids and carve-out condition (c) refuses. THE PER-CLASS QUESTION IS NOW CLOSED TOO — SPP MERIT-ORDER (2026-09-07), at ZERO LP, widening this R from \"uniform quadruple\" to ANY per-band or per-class multiplier set. A per-class curve DERIVED from SPP's own realized prices (one rule, declared before its values: m_c = LW mean measured RT LMP capped at $200 over the hours the MODEL's marginal class is c, / LW mean model price over the same hours, pooled 2023-2025) reads COAL_PRB 0.7838 / COAL_LIGNITE 0.8152 / CC_REGULAR 0.8028 / CT_PEAKER 0.8880 / CT_CHP 0.8019 / ST_GAS 0.8949 / ST_CHP 0.8271 — the whole set spans 0.784-0.895, so SPP's own data says the classes are barely differentiated (peaker-over-coal separation 1.133, +13.3 %, against a ~30 % rotation deficit). On the same pre-registered G-ROT gate it moves the steepening ratio 1.5653 -> 1.6280 (+4.006 %), 1.3306 -> 1.3576 (+2.029 %), 1.6665 -> 1.7217 (+3.312 %) against the required >= +10 %, on an instrument measured to OVER-STATE rotation ~4x — i.e. an expected LP rotation of +0.5 to +1 %, the price-family lane's own measured +0.52 %. It is the same LEVEL lever (LW arm/control 0.8614 / 0.8608 / 0.8522). THE STRUCTURAL REASON, which is the transferable result: THERE IS NO REGIME TO SEPARATE — CT_PEAKER is the marginal class in 24-27 % of SPP's MEDIAN-load hours (cap-weighted over every row within $0.25 of the price) and 49-60 % of its top hours, so any per-class multiplier lifts the middle nearly as much as the top. Related, same lane: pct_peaking is INERT on price for SPP by measurement (all bands 1.0 => a plant's four tranches are price-identical; CT 7.0->40.0 and CC 8.0->30.0 move the LP supply curve by 3.83 MW and total pmax by 5.16 of 59,613 MW). No LP was spent by the merit-order lane. Screen bundle deleted before merge (rule 29(c)); records docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-price-family-2026-09-07.md and docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-merit-order-2026-09-07.md." },
