    measured_interface_limits: { cell: "O", ev: "SPP-40 (2026-09-07) — O: OPEN, first structural evidence on SPP's own data, on the FIRST SPP KEEPER 2026-09-07-spp-1-baseline (bundle spp40_baseline_B; PRECOMMIT-spp-40-2026-09-07.md §3 pushed before the solve; docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-40-2026-09-07.md §2, §7). The SPP-53 N<->S link (3,400 MW, FCITC construction from SPP's own flowgate limits) is LIVE in every year and binds in the measured N->S-dominant direction in two of three: at bound 2023 1,702 h N->S / 275 h S->N, 2024 878 / 897 (a tie — the rule-29(a) 2024 screen's pre-registered direction leg FIRED on that 22-hour margin and the full span was run under owner direction), 2025 1,245 / 373. Link dual ~-6 $/MWh when N->S bound; the model's mean |S-N| zonal spread ~$1 vs the measured $12-17 hub spread (Nebraska-vs-central-Oklahoma two-point spread the two bubbles cannot hold). NOT a verdict on the TTC value, which was NOT moved (rule 14): the 2024 tie is driven by bubble contents (South overnight wind + CC untrapped by the Oklahoma-internal constraints that bind 60-68 % of hours, FINDING-spp-14 §5), not by the pipe's width. Routed to SPP-DESK: FINDING-spp-53 §6 O-1 (asymmetric pair; S->N is live at the symmetric rating) and O-2 (identification width 2,645-11,121 MW); SPP-57 corroborated as the first lever. No other cell moved (rule 28(d)). ||| SPP-57 (2026-09-07, Fable) — STILL O; the THREE-ZONE ARM WAS KILLED at its pre-registered rule-29(a) STOP gate (PRECOMMIT-spp-57-2026-09-07.md §6, pushed at 910fd5b1 before any limit or price was read; FINDING-spp-57-2026-09-07.md §5): an SPP-Oklahoma pocket (OKGE / PSO / GRDA / WFEC; CSWS split by the measured EIA-861 PSO/SWEPCO ratio 0.5216 / 0.5383) in a chain N<->OK<->S, both links rated by the SPP-53 FCITC construction on a three-point spread — N<->OK 6,500 MW (n_s_corridor UNION oklahoma_internal, 26 constituents N->OK-loaded) and OK<->S 6,700 MW (S->OK-loaded, 19 constituents). On the 2025 screen (keeper-2 recipe + topology; 159 s, 5.13 GB) NEITHER LINK IS LIVE: N<->OK at bound 215 h (2.5 % < 5 %), OK<->S 0 h; the S-OK spread sign mismatches (model 0.00 vs measured +11.29); wind re-curtailment 0.00 %; negative-price hours 0 (control 6; measured ~1,000). The union rule pooled western-Oklahoma delivery elements (Gracemont-Anadarko 6,658 h, Cimarron, Woodward) whose binding makes the OKC hub dearer for reasons the hub-pair regression cannot separate from a North->Oklahoma transfer, and the SAME elements identified S->OK on the second link — a double attribution stated in the config comment before the solve and now measured. What the screen's own flows say, reported not re-cut: at the corridor-only 3,400 MW the N<->OK link would sit at/over bound 2,065 h (1,931 N->OK / 134 OK->N — the measured-dominant direction), and at ~3,400 the OK<->S link 622 h (603 S->OK). Full span NOT spent; nothing registered; the topology was NOT landed (solve path restored to the keeper's two zones, byte-identical); the three-zone implementation + the CSWS split + the two new sidecars (rtbm_bc_oklahoma_limits_2026.parquet, actual_lmp_hourly_area_SPP.parquet) + data/raw/eia-861 stay on the branch / in the tree for a re-issue with corridor-only N<->OK (SPP-53's 3,400) and an OK<->S rating from the SPS-tie set (SPP-54/58's object). NOT a keeper candidate (owner asked in-session; answered: no — structure regressed, the keeper's 3,400 MW binding is what the arm lost). ||| SPP-57b (2026-09-07, Fable) — STILL O; the RE-ISSUE with the constituent sets re-declared ex ante (PRECOMMIT-spp-57b-2026-09-07.md §3, pushed at 42ed8ff6 before any number was derived; FINDING-spp-57b-2026-09-07.md §0) was KILLED at the same rule-29(a) STOP gate on 2025: N<->OK rated by n_s_corridor ALONE = SPP-53's 3,400 MW unchanged, OK<->S by sps_tie ALONE on (p_S - p_OK) = 10,700 MW OK->S-named (4 identified constituents, 6,177 h, zero S->OK-identified; the rule's weighted median, not the desk's expected 3,000-4,000), oklahoma_internal EXCLUDED from both by a group rule. Screen (keeper-2 recipe + topology; 211.9 s, 4.93 GB): the corridor-only N<->OK link IS live — at bound 2,061 h (23.5 %), 1,920 N->OK / 141 OK->N (93.2 %), confirming SPP-57 §5.3's 2,065 in a second solve — but OK<->S never binds (0 h): the model's residual South (SPS wind + SWEPCO thermal on one copperplate) EXPORTS into Oklahoma in every hour above the median (flow p50 -1,188 / p1 -4,682 MW; OK->S max +3,133) while the SPS ties identify OK->S-loaded (they bind on imports INTO the Panhandle; measured S-OK +11.29), so no OK->S-named rating >= 3,400 can be live in its own direction (at ~3,400 it would be live 638 h, all S->OK, failing the direction leg). S-OK sign mismatch (0.00 vs +11.29), re-curtailment 0.00 %, unserved 89 -> 444 MWh (new hour h8508, attributed to the per-zone wind-shape rebuild at identical demand / pipe / system wind), negative hours 4 (control 6; ~1,018 measured). Full span NOT spent; nothing registered; topology NOT landed (solve path restored byte-identical; the (B') implementation is design commit 7bfe047d). NOT a keeper candidate under the standing structure-first rule: one link went inert -> live-and-directed, the other stayed inert, the pocket traps nothing. Routed: R-17 the residual-bubble split (SPP-54, re-ranked ahead of any third re-issue), R-18 the unserved rise, R-19/R-20 the asymmetric pair and the psi width (SPP-58). ||| SPP-58 (2026-09-07, Fable) — STILL O; ZERO-LP; the SECOND, INDEPENDENT shift-factor identification (PRECOMMIT-spp-58-2026-09-07.md pushed at da1bb516 before any PTDF; FINDING-spp-58-2026-09-07.md §0): psi_2 = a DC-network PTDF/OTDF on public HIFLD line geometry (17,873 features, 2023 vintage) + EIA-860 plants, generator-weighted bubble-to-bubble pairs, price-free (option (a) unavailable: no flow column in the served RTBM schema; option (b) absent: the Public Data Guide v35 lists no shift-factor product). Interconnection cleaning verified by EIA-860 BA codes; K1-K4 hold (cut-set identities 1.000, line sign agreement 7/8). OUTSIDE the declared 1.92x band on EVERY object: N->S like-for-like T*_2 11,022 vs T*_1 4,919 (same subset) and vs the standing 3,400 (psi_2 lands on psi_1's drop-2024 fold 11,121); S->N 13,175 vs 4,206; sps_tie 1,600 vs 10,705 (the SPS ties ARE the cut-set: 8 crossing branches carry 1.000 of the South-rest->SPS transfer, SPPSPSTIES 0.853 with 6/9 elements, so T* ~ limit-at-bind). By the rule ttc_mw is UNTOUCHED (3,400 stands) and the desk holds the card (R-21/R-22). Potter County width COLLAPSED (psi_2 0.369 OTDF / 0.311 PTDF = 1.19; OTDF > PTDF, the reverse of psi_1's 0.047 < 0.132). Double attribution of the western-Oklahoma elements is REAL physics (Cimarron / Woodward / Cornville load on both bubble transfers) — SPP-57b's exclusion stands. Franklin 161/69, 44 % of the corridor's binding hours and psi_1's median, is UNRESOLVABLE (no sub-115 kV public line data, R-23). Structural reading: psi_1 assigns the 115/161 kV under-lay elements sensitivities (0.035-0.365) the topology does not support (<= 0.026); the 345 kV backbone agrees in sign and order. SPP-54's rating input: 1,600 MW. No mechanism tested, no cell moved." },
